.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
vector_db/
# The image's store, written from vector_db/ by scripts/export_runtime_db.py.
vector_db_runtime/
logs/
preprocessed_db/
uploads/
.DS_Store
*.egg-info/

# `python -m leasehound.scan <lease>` defaults to --out scan_report.md, so running
# the README's own command dirties the working tree. Anchored to the root on
# purpose: examples/scan_report.md is the committed example output and must stay
# tracked, and an unanchored pattern would match it at any depth.
/scan_report.md

# Real published lease PDFs: third-party documents, fetched on demand from
# evaluation/leases_real/sources.json. The manifest and results are tracked.
evaluation/leases_real/*.pdf

# Personal interview prep lives on the Desktop, not here. This line is a guard: if a
# file by that name ever reappears in the repo, it must not reach a public commit.
INTERVIEW.md

# The Chinese reading aid's cache (evaluation/review_generation.py --zh). A machine
# translation of statute text, regenerable and not evidence of anything: the audit is
# conducted against the English, which is why the gloss is printed beneath it rather
# than instead of it. Committing 243 KB of it would put a model's paraphrase of the law
# in a directory whose whole point is that its contents are measurements.
evaluation/review_gloss_zh.json
